      "authority_mode": "world_author",
      "prose": "The last of the rain whispered against the dispensary window. Mara lifted the striped glass flask from the oak counter. She opened its hinged cap, then snapped the cap shut. \"Take the striped one; I will take the dotted one,\" she told Eren. In one exchange, she handed him the striped flask while taking the dotted flask from his hand. Eren set the striped flask on the counter and let go. \"Yesterday you said, 'Open the dotted one,'\" he remarked, leaving both caps shut. Mara put the dotted flask on the low stool and released it. Eren lifted the striped flask from the counter, then passed it back to Mara. \"Both can wait here,\" she said. She set the striped flask beside the dotted flask on the stool and let go. The oak counter itself had not moved.",
