      "prose": "Dust shone in the slant of afternoon light above the maple bench. Neri picked up the short silver key, leaving the long silver key where it lay. \"Try the short one first,\" Olan said. Keeping her fingers around its bow, Neri pushed the short key partway into the red cashbox's lock; its tip entered the keyway, but its shoulder stopped outside. She tried to turn the key, but it would not rotate and the cashbox stayed locked and shut. \"Wrong key,\" she said. She pulled the short key completely out of the lock. Then she laid it on the bench and released it. Olan picked up the long silver key and, after a pause, set it back beside the short one and let go. \"Neither has opened it,\" he said.",
