      "authority_mode": "world_author",
      "prose": "Noa's violet rehearsal coat caught on the chair until she stepped clear of it. \"Hold this a moment,\" she told Kit. She took the coat off, held it in both hands, and passed it to Kit. Kit laid it across the slatted chair and released it. Noa picked up the white cloakroom ticket from the narrow shelf and handed it to Kit. \"The ticket, not the coat, is yours,\" she said. Kit set the ticket back on the shelf, then lifted the coat from the chair and handed the coat back to Noa. Noa put the same violet coat on and let her hands fall free. She walked through the open doorway onto the landing. Kit stayed beside the chair. \"It fits again,\" Noa said from the landing.",
